## 5. Contributor Records

The Owner may maintain a Contributor Record identifying individuals or entities whose Contributions have been incorporated into the Work.

A Contributor Record may contain:

* the Contributor's name or chosen identifier;
* a summary of the Contributor's work;
* the date or version in which the Contribution was incorporated; and
* other information reasonably related to acknowledging the Contribution.

A Contributor Record exists solely for attribution and record-keeping purposes.

A Contributor Record does not grant the Contributor ownership, control, governance rights, voting rights, royalties, payment, management authority, or any other additional rights in the Work or project.

The inclusion of a person or entity in a Contributor Record does not create a partnership, joint ownership arrangement, employment relationship, agency relationship, or other legal relationship with the Owner.

The Owner may correct, update, reorganize, or remove entries in a Contributor Record when reasonably necessary to maintain accurate project records.

